{{ html }}


{% if product.title contains "Snowboard" %}
    <p>This contains snowboard</p>
{% endif %}

{% comment %} unless is opposite of contains {% endcomment %}
{% unless product.tags contains "Premium" %}
    <p>This doesn't contains Premium tags</p>
{% else %}
    <p>This contains Premium tags </p>
{% endunless %}

{% comment %}
 Shopify Liquid checks the conditions from the right to left:
 product.title contains "Snowboard" or product.title == "snowboard" and product.price < 100
 product.title contains "Snowboard" or product.title == "snowboard" and False
 product.title contains "Snowboard" or True and False
 product.title contains "Snowboard" or False
 True or False
 True

 That's why its an anomaly.
 So we use an extra variable check for it.
{% endcomment %}

{% assign is_snowboard = false %}
{% if product.title contains "Snowboard" or product.title == "snowboard" %}
  {% assign is_snowboard = true %}
{% endif %}

{% if is_snowboard and product.price < 70000 %}
  <p>This is an affordable snowboard</p>
{% endif %}

{% comment %}
    To check if a string is empty we use "blank" object
    Whereas, nil for undefined values.
{% endcomment %}

{% if product.type != blank %}
    {% case product.type %}
        {% when "snowboard" %}
            <p>This is a snowboard </p>
        {% when "gift card" %}
            <p>This is gift card</p>
        {% when "ski wax" %}
            <p>This is ski wax</p>
        {% else %}
            <p>BAM BAM</p>
    {% endcase %}
{% endif %}
